  "id": "COMPOUND:21166 - PROTEIN:1503",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a direct relationship between (2E,6E)-3,7,11-Trimethyl-9-(phenylsulfonyl)-2,6,10-dodecatrien-1-ol and G1/S-specific cyclin-D1, through a series of target interactions involving Cytochrome c4. This compound appears to act as a target for multiple compounds, including 6-O-Acetyldihydrohelenalin and 5-O-Demethylpaxanthonin, which in turn target cyclin-D1. The shared involvement of Cytochrome c4 in these pathways indicates a potential mechanism where the compound may influence cyclin-D1 expression or activity through a common downstream effector. The consistent presence of Cytochrome c4 as a target in all three paths suggests a functional link that could involve post-translational modifications or regulatory pathways. The evidence supports a plausible mechanism where the compound may modulate cyclin-D1 through a pathway involving Cytochrome c4, though the exact nature of this interaction remains to be elucidated.",
